VALUES (634, '0', $t$ASK 634: a judge's corrected FORCED line is applied at that pair's FORCED line when the line it flagged is not in its text$t$,
  $t$In run 42528 sol's send-back changes S9, S10 and S14 flagged a line that is sol's own pointer and was never in sol's judgment text, so the apply refused each one ("the flagged line is not in the judge text", NOT APPLIED). At the gate (G2, G3, G7) sol answered each with CHANGE TO and a whole FORCED line for the same pair, and the re-apply anchored on the same missing line and failed again; the items stayed UNCURED and counted in drv_uncured, and no CHANGE TO could have cured them (enforcer rows 54568, 54569, 54573). Change, Shared Library sbApply2024 (LIB 1426): when the flagged line is not found and the change is a FORCED line for a named pair, it is applied at the one FORCED line of that pair in the judge's text; with no such line, or more than one, it stays NOT APPLIED as before. This is the rule the engine already uses for a RETRACTED change. Expected effect on 42528: G2, G3 and G7 would be applied and CURED, sol's drv_uncured 9 to 6, the outcome unchanged. Not changed: reasoning, a model setting, a prompt, a count rule, what a judge is sent. (plan rev 0, heading 1, ask634/w4/plan634.md md5 4735a147)$t$,
  'in part',
  $t$Written by W4 on the operator's press "Write it" at 08:35 CST 2026-11-25 on W4's card (Wall 12082; audit 42241 by W4's facts file), engine e11a57aa to 7f4e5503, after W1's recheck PASS of the rebased target b4 e6d00811 (Wall 12078), and read back PASS by W1 (Wall 12085: live 7f4e5503 equals W1's b4 rebuild in all 426 nodes; t634 22 pass 0 fail; standing 31 PASS 0 FAIL). Shared Library only, one LIB line (1426); 13 MAP lengths re-measured; nothing was deleted. IN PART, because no run has been made since the write. This change moves items from UNCURED to CURED, which feeds drv_uncured and seat removal: W1's N1 on the plan (Wall 12002) asked for the effect on the verdict, and it is met (Wall 12009): sol's stored verdict_raw for 42528 has exactly one line-start FORCED line for each of D3 vs C4, D5 vs C2 and D6 vs C1; sol's drv_uncured goes from 9 to 6, sol stays unseated and the outcome does not change (NOT CHECKED by W1: the stored 9). The written target is the fourth rebase of one unchanged build script: the first build on 3b72583c (5309a11f, PASS, Wall 12009), b1 on ee4e389d (2136d5ad, checked, Wall 12046), b2 on the 641 fetch-back (7a19c8be; W4 found no W1 post naming it), b3 on the 645 fetch-back (56ea8c28, PASS, Wall 12076), b4 on the 646 fetch-back (e6d00811, PASS, Wall 12078); in each the one changed line is byte-equal to the graded text. NOT CHECKED by W1: enforcer rows 54568, 54569 and 54573 (plan grade); the audit row. Open: two clean live runs. RUN REVISION 43103 (this row; where a sentence above says that no run has been made, this paragraph is the later word): run ODV1-43103-gkg7el4e (debate_results 0731a1ea, row saved 11:20 CST 2026-11-27; the operator's launch 10:48 CST, ended 11:44 CST by W4's report, Wall 12767; engine 66ba992d and child aad0ad9c; google/gemini-4-hydrogen as the Oracle defending against meta/muse-spark-1.3; outcome UNGRADED, panel 0-0 with 3 not counted under the debate rule; three judgments stored (sonnet, sol, sol62); cost 7.5384; no debate_errors row after the launch). NOT EXERCISED. No enforcer row of the run says "flagged line is not in the judge text" (W4; W1 by SQL: 0 of 503 rows), so the case of run 42528 did not arise. W3 does not count this run as one of the two live runs with no issue; objective_met and status are unchanged.$t$,
  '12002, 12009, 12043, 12046, 12069, 12075, 12076, 12077, 12078, 12082, 12085, 12121, 12128, 12129, 12142, 12787, 12791, 12797, 12799, 12800, 12802, 12803, 12804, 12789',
